# corlogic known-difference filter. One entry per line; a matching finding is muted.
#
# Two forms:
#   CATEGORY|MECHANISM|CONSTRUCTS|STATEMENT   a UID pattern. A field of * matches
#                                             anything, a field ending in * matches by
#                                             prefix, and a field wrapped in * matches
#                                             anywhere in the value, so one line mutes a
#                                             family
#   <12 hex>                                  one exact testcase, by its testcase id
# A full "<id>//<UID>" line as printed in a report counts as both.
#
# CONSTRUCTS is a set of tokens, comma separated and sorted alphabetically. Match it with
# the wrapped form, *CTE*, which finds the token wherever it sits. A prefix, CTE*, only
# matches when that token happens to sort first, so it silently misses most statements.
# The wrapped form is anchored on the commas there, so *IN* is the token IN and never the
# IN inside INSERT.
#
# The UID of a finding is the "UID:" line of its bugN.report, and `pr` in the workdir
# prints it as well.
#
# An entry that names one statement does not hide the same defect reached another way. A
# finding that agrees with such an entry on the category and the mechanism, on a statement
# the entry does not name, is still reported, and the report says which entry it sits
# beside so it can go on that ticket instead of becoming a new bug. A comment above an
# entry naming an MDEV or MENT number puts that number in the notice. The notice needs a
# mechanism that names both sides, an error pair or an affected-count pair among them. A
# mechanism naming neither side, content and coltype for example, is shared by too much to
# say anything, so it gets no notice.
#
# corlogic.known.INFO carries the long form: one section per entry with the cause, the
# code citations and the evidence, including the entries that live in a sibling known
# file. Read it before adding an entry here.

# ANALYZE TABLE reports its own progress differently per version; the statistics refresh
# in the stream is compared on state alone, but a generated ANALYZE inside a testcase can
# still land here.
RESULT|content|*|ANALYZE TABLE*

# A plan whose only difference is the access type on a table with no index is the
# optimizer choosing between two equal-cost paths.
PLAN|ALL>index|*|*

# MDEV-37939, the logarithm domain error. As described in corlogic.known.INFO.
ERROR|1365v3047|*|*

# MDEV-40877, wrong result from NOT IN with a NULL in a materialized subquery. As
# described in corlogic.known.INFO.
4609a4ba3fe6//RESULT|rows0v26|IN,SUBQ|SELECT * FROM tX o WHERE o.cX NOT IN (SELECT cX FROM tX) LIMIT N

# MDEV-36166, MULTIPOINT WKT with brackets is not read. As described in
# corlogic.known.INFO.
791a7ad99edf//RESULT|content|SPATIAL|SELECT ST_ASTEXT(ST_UNION(ST_GEOMFROMTEXT('X'), ST_GEOMFROMTEXT('Y')))

# MDEV-27310, ONLY_FULL_GROUP_BY is not applied to the ORDER BY list. As described in
# corlogic.known.INFO.
ERROR|1055v0|*ORDERBY*|*
ERROR|0v1140|*ORDERBY*|*

# MDEV-11588, no functional-dependency detection for ONLY_FULL_GROUP_BY. As described in
# corlogic.known.INFO.
3962a83db959//ERROR|0v1140|AGG|SELECT COUNT(*),cX FROM tX WHERE cX=N AND cX IS NOT NULL
